WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.887
Week 24: Commands, Advice, and Procedures. give a safe procedure offer advice distinguish request from order

2
00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:22.433
Form and meaning. Applying the form. Tú commands use the usted-form for negative (no compartas) but a special affirmative form; usted/ustedes commands use the opposite-vowel ending; nosotros commands mean let's.

3
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:45.705
Model set. Apaga la luz, por favor. Apague el sistema con cuidado. Apaguen todos los equipos. Apaguemos las pantallas antes de salir. No compartas la contraseña. Turn off the light, please. Turn off the system carefully. Turn off all the equipment. Let's turn off the screens before leaving. Don't share the password.

4
00:00:45.705 --> 00:00:55.856
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:55.856 --> 00:01:07.906
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: give a safe procedure; offer advice; distinguish request from order. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:07.906 --> 00:01:31.881
Model language. Apaga la luz, por favor. — Turn off the light, please. Apague el sistema con cuidado. — Turn off the system carefully. Apaguen todos los equipos. — Turn off all the equipment. Apaguemos las pantallas antes de salir. — Let's turn off the screens before leaving. No compartas la contraseña. — Don't share the password.

7
00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:41.779
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
